WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:05.071
This is Jarvis, an assistant I built that runs on my own computer.

2
00:00:05.967 --> 00:00:07.417
It runs on localhost.

3
00:00:07.417 --> 00:00:11.079
You bring your own key, and it stays on your machine.

4
00:00:11.967 --> 00:00:15.065
Simple commands never wait for a model.

5
00:00:15.065 --> 00:00:19.911
Jarvis matches them directly, in English, Tanglish and Tamil.

6
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.203
Everything else goes to a model:

7
00:00:23.203 --> 00:00:27.482
Claude, Gemini, or a local model when the internet drops.

8
00:00:27.482 --> 00:00:31.386
It picks from a hundred and three tools, for memory,

9
00:00:31.386 --> 00:00:34.840
reminders, routines, files and a second brain.

10
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:38.118
And it can't do damage by accident.

11
00:00:38.118 --> 00:00:40.844
Dangerous commands are blocked outright.

12
00:00:40.844 --> 00:00:43.160
Risky ones stop and ask, by click,

13
00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.954
by voice, or a thumbs down to the camera.

14
00:00:45.954 --> 00:00:47.589
Deletes go to the Trash.

15
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.851
It has more than fifteen hundred automated tests,

16
00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.287
and it's open source.

17
00:00:53.287 --> 00:00:54.860
The link is on my site.

